    "markdown": "---\nengine: knitr\n---\n\n# Recap\n![](/images/question_bubble_red.png){style=\"width:150px\" fig-align=\"center\"}\n\nBrilliant! You've gone through all the advanced Linux practice.\nThe next page contains an exercise.\nBefore that there is a little information on permissions followed by some recap MCQs.\n\n\n## Permissions\nAll files, directories and programs have permissions. It is important to know about this so you know your read, write and executability permissions for the content within machines.\n\nBelow is a useful link to learn about file permissions:  \n<https://www.guru99.com/file-permissions.html>\n\n## MCQs\n\nPlease attempt to answer the below Multiple-Choice Questions to reinforce what you have learnt in this part.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n1.  Which symbol is used to pipe the output of one command to the input of another? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_FQGIXSWIAE'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_FQGIXSWIAE\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`>`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_FQGIXSWIAE\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>__`|`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_FQGIXSWIAE\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`sed`__</span></label></div>\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n2.  What command can be used to substitute text with other text? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_FBRCGMLGGK'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_FBRCGMLGGK\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`>`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_FBRCGMLGGK\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`|`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_FBRCGMLGGK\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>__`sed`__</span></label></div>\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n3.  Which symbol is used to redirect the output of a command to a file? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_QUIDNMFQZN'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_QUIDNMFQZN\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>__`>`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_QUIDNMFQZN\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`|`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_QUIDNMFQZN\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`sed`__</span></label></div>\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n4. Which wildcard represents a single character? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_SNZWCAXOAS'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_SNZWCAXOAS\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`*`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_SNZWCAXOAS\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`[]`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_SNZWCAXOAS\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>__`?`__</span></label></div>\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n5. Which wildcard represents zero or more characters? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_RFIYPSQJRY'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_RFIYPSQJRY\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>__`*`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_RFIYPSQJRY\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`[]`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_RFIYPSQJRY\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`?`__</span></label></div>\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n6. Which wildcard represents a range of characters? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_PSYFLKIVMU'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_PSYFLKIVMU\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`*`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_PSYFLKIVMU\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>__`[]`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_PSYFLKIVMU\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`?`__</span></label></div>\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n7. Which regular expression indicates that the preceding character matches 1 or 0 times? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_VXYCSFUIEZ'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_VXYCSFUIEZ\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`.`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_VXYCSFUIEZ\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>__`?`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_VXYCSFUIEZ\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`*`__</span></label></div>\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n8. Which regular expression represents a single character?  <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_PTCSWHYXXF'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_PTCSWHYXXF\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>__`.`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_PTCSWHYXXF\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`?`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_PTCSWHYXXF\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`*`__</span></label></div>\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n9. Which regular expression indicates that the preceding character matches zero or more times? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_KXLSCHNEEN'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_KXLSCHNEEN\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`.`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_KXLSCHNEEN\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`?`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_KXLSCHNEEN\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>__`*`__</span></label></div>\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n10. Which regular expression matches the end of the line? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_JPKLMTARDY'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_JPKLMTARDY\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`|`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_JPKLMTARDY\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`^`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_JPKLMTARDY\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>__`$`__</span></label></div>\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n11. Which regular expression is a logical OR operator? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_IFYMPWOIIN'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_IFYMPWOIIN\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>__`|`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_IFYMPWOIIN\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`^`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_IFYMPWOIIN\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`$`__</span></label></div>\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n12. Which regular expression matches the start of the line? <div class='webex-radiogroup' id='radio_OVBPTQXHKB'><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_OVBPTQXHKB\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`|`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_OVBPTQXHKB\" value=\"answer\"></input> <span>__`^`__</span></label><label><input type=\"radio\" autocomplete=\"off\" name=\"radio_OVBPTQXHKB\" value=\"\"></input> <span>__`$`__</span></label></div>\n",
